problem:
The grid below contains six rows with six points in each row. Points that are adjacent either horizontally or vertically are a distance of 2 units apart. Find the area of the irregularly shaped ten-sided figure shown.

\[\text{[asy]}\]
\text{import graph; size(5cm);}
\text{pen dps = linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(10); defaultpen(dps);}
\text{pen dotstyle = black;}
\text{draw((-2,5)--(-3,4), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((-3,4)--(-2,1), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((-2,1)--(1,0), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((1,0)--(2,1), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((2,1)--(1,3), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((1,3)--(1,4), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((1,4)--(2,5), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((2,5)--(0,5), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((-2,5)--(-1,4), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{draw((-1,4)--(0,5), linewidth(1.6));}
\text{dot((-3,5),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
\text{dot((-2,5),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
\text{dot((-1,5),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
\text{dot((0,5),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
\text{dot((1,5),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
\text{dot((2,5),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
\text{dot((2,4),linewidth(6pt) + dotstyle);}
